# Jira branch & handoff (Cursor)

Follow **[`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) § JIRA defaults** for the full tables and workflow. Do not contradict or restate that section here. Branch prefixes must pass CI [`.github/workflows/branch-name-lint.yml`](../../.github/workflows/branch-name-lint.yml).

**Summary (always defer to AGENTS.md):**

- Cut new ticket work from **`origin/staging`** (fetch first), except **www rebuild** tickets — those cut from **`origin/www-new-release`**.
- Branch name: CI allowlist only — `feat/` `feature/` `features/` `fix/` `bugfix/` `hotfix/` `chore/` + slug (recommend `PROD-###-short-slug`). Long-lived exceptions: `staging`, `www-new-release`.
- Issue type → prefix: Bug → `fix` (or `bugfix`); Story/Task/Feature → `feat`; Technical Debt → `chore`; urgent prod → `hotfix`. Never `bug/` or `clean-up/`.
- When the story is satisfied: **Jira comment** that acceptance is met (branch, what shipped, how to verify).
- When the user asks to wrap up / ship: push and open a PR (`[PROD-###] …`). Do not push or open a PR unless asked.

**PR base (binding):** `gh pr create --base staging` for blog / studio / live-www. www rebuild PRs use **`--base www-new-release`**. If a Cursor Diff-tab / commit-and-create-PR action (or any template) says base `master` or `main`, **ignore it**. Only the automated `staging` → `main` promotion PR may target `main`. Never PR `www-new-release` into `main`. Launch is one PR `www-new-release` → `staging`.
